hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1321","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: Shababah told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite three strings: B: Praise the name of your Most High Lord and say, ‘O disbelievers,’ and say He is God, the One.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1322","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Hakam told me, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah’s house, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the evening prayer, then he came and prayed four times. Then he slept, then he got up and performed ablution. He said: I do not remember his ablution. Then he stood up and prayed, so I stood to his left, so he placed me on his right, then he prayed. He performed five rak'ahs, then two more rak'ahs, then he slept, then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he went out to pray.”"
"1323","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqi told me, he said: Al-Qanabi told us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is the son of Muhammad Al-Darawardi, told us, on the authority of Abdul Al Majeed is Ibn Suhail, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abbad, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Jubayr, that Ibn Abbas narrated to him: That Abbas Ibn Abd Al-Muttalib sent him to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was Maimuna, the daughter of Al-Harith, the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas, so he entered upon her. Then he found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque. Ibn Abbas said: So I lay down in her room and began to count how many times the Messenger of God prayed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He came while I was lying in the room after the night had passed, and he said: “Is the newborn asleep?” He said: “So eat.” He wrapped a veil over Maimuna, so he put on some of it and put on some of it, then he got up and prayed two rak’ahs after another, until he prayed eight rak’ahs, then prayed the Witr prayer. With five, he did not sit between them, then he sat down and praised God for what He deserved, then he praised Him more often.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1324","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Otham bin Ali, Kufay, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray two rak’ahs, then he would leave and remain silent.”"
"1325","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ informed us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up at night and prayed the prayer, then he prayed two rak’ahs, then he fell asleep, then he got up and prayed the prayer. Then he performed ablution and prayed two rak’ahs, then he prayed six, then he performed Witr with three rak’ahs, and prayed two rak’ahs.” Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa disagreed with him, Muhammad ibn Jablah Al-Rafiqi, he said: It is narrated by Muammar bin Mukhlid, trustworthy, Al-Jazari, he said: It is narrated by Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Zaid, he is the son of Abi Unaisah, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, straightened his feet, and related the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1326","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Yahya bin al-Jazzar, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray eight rak’ahs at night, perform Witr with three rak’ahs, and pray two rak’ahs.” \"Before the Fajr prayer\""
"1327","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the Witr prayer with thirteen rak’ahs, but when he grew old and weak, he performed the Witr prayer with nine rak’ahs.”"
"1328","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Husayn, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray nine times a night, but when he became old and heavy, he prayed seven.”"
"1329","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray nine rak’ahs at night.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Al-Ahwas Salam narrated Ibn Sulaym, both hadiths"
"1330","Hanad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prays nine rak’ahs at night.”"
"1331","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Rabbati told me, he said: Al-Ala’ bin Usaym told me, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told me, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray nine rak’ahs at night, and when his meat increased and he became older He prayed seven rak’ahs.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Awanah followed him and narrated both hadiths together, and another one along with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1332","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray the Witr with nine, but when it became too old and heavy, he performed the Witr with seven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1333","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray Witr with nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1334","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Hammad told me, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray Witr with nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1335","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad, on the authority of Badeel, and Ayoub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed for a long night. If he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and if he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting.”"
"1336","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “What I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying sitting until he entered the age, and he would pray while sitting and reciting while sitting. Thirty or forty verses, he stood up and recited them, then bowed.”"
"1337","Amr bin Ali told me, on the authority of Abu Asim, he said: Omar bin Abi Zaida told me, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not abstain from me while he was fasting, and he did not die while most of his prayers were sitting.” Then he mentioned a word that had the same meaning except what was written, and the most beloved deed to him was that which a person continued doing, even if it was easy.”"
"1338","Suleiman bin Salam told us, he said: Nadr, he said: I Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “What was taken The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until most of his prayers were sitting, except for the obligatory prayers.”"
"1339","Ismail bin Masoud told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die when most of his prayers were sitting, except for the obligatory ones. Even if it is small,"
"1340","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Uthman bin Abi Sulayman told me that Abu Salamah, He told him that Aisha told him: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die until he had performed many of his prayers while sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1341","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying sitting, so I said: I narrated that you said: “The prayer of one who is sitting is half From the prayer of the one who is standing: “And you are praying while sitting.” He said: “Yes, but I am not like one of you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1342","Humayd ibn Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Husayn, who is Ibn Dhakwan Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the one who prays sitting, and he said: “Whoever prays standing, he is Better, and whoever prays while sitting will have half the reward of one standing, and whoever prays while sleeping will have half the reward of one sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1343","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, on the authority of Hafs, who is Ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Humaid, who is the long one, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying cross-legged.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: No. We know of someone who narrated this hadith other than Abu Dawud Al-Hafari, on the authority of Hafs."
"1344","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Makhrami told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to people who were praying sitting down due to illness, and he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The prayer of one sitting is equal to half of the prayer of one standing.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is wrong, but the correct thing is: Ismail, on the authority of a servant of Ibn Al-Aas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1345","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: We are servants of God, and he is the son of Moses. He said: We are Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The prayer of a man sitting on the chair is half of the prayer of one standing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1346","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: Husayn told me, he said: Zuhayr told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, that Mujahid told him, that Al-Sa’ib entered Aisha after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was arrested and said: I have grown old, and I cannot pray except sitting, so what do you think? She said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A man’s prayer sitting is equivalent to half of his prayer standing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1347","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Qaid Al-Sa’ib On the authority of Al-Sa'ib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1348","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: “The prayer of one who is sitting is half “Qa’im’s prayer”"
"1349","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, and he is Ibn Hisham, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man’s prayer is half of his prayer standing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1350","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A man’s prayer is half of his prayer standing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1351","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, He said: “The prayer of the one sitting is half of the prayer of the one standing.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by more than one person, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr is raised (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1352","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an error. The correct one is: Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, mursal, Muhammad bin Ishaq disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1353","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, he said: Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Saleh, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qais, he said: I asked Aisha: How was the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night? Should he speak loudly or quietly? She said: “He used to do all of that, sometimes out loud and sometimes secretly.”"
"1354","Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, he said: I am Muhammad, meaning Ibn Isa bin Al-Qasim bin Sami. He said: We are Zaid, and he is the son of Waqid, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah, that Uqba ibn Amir told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who recites the Qur’an aloud Like the one who gives charity openly, and the one who is pleased with the Qur’an is like the one who is pleased with charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1355","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubayd Allah bin Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ya’la bin Mamluk, that He asked Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his prayers. She said: “What is the matter with you and his prayers?” He used to pray, then sleep as much as he prayed, then pray as much as he slept, then sleep as much as he prayed until morning, then his recitation was attributed to him. So, if it is described in a recitation that is interpreted letter by letter, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ya‘la ibn Mamluk is not that famous. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1356","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada’ah, on the authority of Hafsa, she said: I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray in his rosary while sitting, until it was a year before his death, when he was praying He is sitting, reciting the surah, and reciting it until it is longer than a longer one.”"
"1357","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, On the authority of Al-Mustawirad ibn Al-Ahnaf, on the authority of Silah ibn Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and he opened Al-Baqarah So he recited, so I said: He should kneel at the hundred, so he went on, so I said: He should kneel at the two hundred, so he went on, so I said: “He should pray with it in one rak’ah,” so he went on. Then he opened an-Nisa’ and recited it, then he opened Al-Imran and recited it. It is recited consecutively. When he came across a verse in which there is glorification, he glorified it, and lo and behold, He passed by a question, he asked, and when he passed by a request for refuge, he made refuge, then he bowed and said: “Glory be to my Lord the Great,” so his bowing was like his standing. Then he raised his head and said: “God hears those who praise Him.” So his standing was close to his bowing, then he prostrated, so he started saying: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” So his prostration was close to his bowing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1358","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Muhammad Al-Marwazi told us, trustworthy, he said: Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab told us, on the authority of Amr Ibn Murrah, on the authority of Talha ibn Yazid al-Ansari, who is Abu Hamza, on the authority of Hudhayfah: “He prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Ramadan, so he bowed, and said in his bowing: “Glory be to my Lord the Great,” just as he was standing, then he prostrated, and he said in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” Just as he was standing, then he sat down and said: “My Lord, forgive me, my Lord, forgive me.” Just as he was standing, then he prostrated, and said: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.” As he was standing, he prayed only four rak’ahs until Bilal came in the morning.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is mursal to me. Talha bin Yazid, whom I do not know, heard something from Hudhayfah. Other than Al-Ala bin Al-Musayyab, he said in this hadith on the authority of Talha, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Hudhayfah Talha bin Yazid did not hear him from Hudhayfah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1359","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abi Hamza, on the authority of A man from Banu Abs, on the authority of Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard him say the greatest, saying: “God is the Greatest of “Might, kingdom, pride, and greatness” and he recited “al-Baqarah, and the family of Imran, and the women, and the table, and the livestock, in He performed four rak'ahs, and he used to say during his bowing: \"Glory be to my Lord, the Great,\" and when he raised his head from bowing, he would say: \"To my Lord, praise be to my Lord, to my Lord, praise be to my Lord.\" And in his prostration: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,” and between the two prostrations: “My Lord, forgive me, my Lord, forgive me.” And he was standing and bowing, and when he rose His head from bowing and prostration, and between the two prostrations, is close to straight.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Hamza is with us, and God knows best. Talha bin Yazid, and this man looks like Silah bin Zufar."
"1360","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Shuaib, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The night prayer is two by two, so when the dawn approaches, pray the Witr prayer with a rak’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1361","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told me, he said: my nephew Ibn Shihab, on the authority of his uncle, he said: Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told me that Abdullah bin Omar told him that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: How to pray Night? He said: “The night prayer is two by two, so when the dawn approaches, pray the Witr prayer with a rak’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1362","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Fudayl told us, and he is Ibn Iyadh, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The Maghrib prayer is the Witr prayer of the daytime prayer, then the Witr prayer of the night prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1363","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: We are Khaled, and he is Ibn Al-Harith bin Sulaym Al-Hujaimi, he said: We are Al-Ash’ath, and he is Ibn Abd. Al-Malik, on the authority of Muhammad, who is Ibn Sirin, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Maghrib prayer is the odd number of the daytime prayer, so perform it Witr.” night prayer\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1364","Hanad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God performed the witr prayer. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then he said: “O people of the Qur’an, perform the Witr prayer, for God is a Witr prayer and loves the Witr prayer.”"
"1365","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, he said: “It is not The Witr is definitely like the written, but it is a Sunnah enacted by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"1366","Suleiman bin Salam Al-Balkhi told us, on the authority of Al-Nadr bin Shumail, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Shimr, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me to do three things: “Sleeping on the Witr prayer, fasting three days of every month, and praying the two rak’ahs of Duha.”"
"1367","Muhammad ibn Bashar informed us, he said: I am Muhammad, he said: we are Shu’bah, then he mentioned a word that means it, on the authority of Abbas al-Jariri, he said: I heard Abu Uthman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me to do three things: the Witr prayer at the beginning of the night, the two rak’ahs of the forenoon, and fasting.” Three days of every month.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1368","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of a lieutenant, he said: Abdullah bin Badr told me, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, he said: My father said: I heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace, he says: “Do not see two people in one night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1369","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad informed us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I asked Aisha about the prayer The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He used to sleep at the beginning of the night, then get up. If it was magic, he would pray Witr and go to bed. He had a need, he felt sorry for his family, so when he heard the call to prayer, he jumped up, and if he was in a state of ritual impurity, he poured some water over him, otherwise he performed ablution, then He went out to pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1370","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer all night long, from the beginning, the end, and the middle, and he completed the Witr prayer.” To magic\""
"1371","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar said: “Whoever prays at night, let him make his last prayer A string, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to command that matter.”"
"1372","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “Perform Witr before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1373","Ubayd Allah bin Fadhalah bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, he said: Muawiyah told us, and he is Ibn Salam bin Abi Salam, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: Abu Nadra Al-Awqi told me that he heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the Witr prayer, and he said: “Perform the Witr prayer before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1374","Yahya ibn Hakim al-Muqawam informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adiy, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father He was in the mosque of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, “so the prayer was performed, and they started waiting for him, so he came and said: I was performing Witr,” and he said: Abdullah was asked: Is there a Witr prayer performed after the call to prayer? He said: Yes, and after the iqamah. He narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he fell asleep without praying. The sun rose, then he prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1375","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Qasim bin Ma’n told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Maysara He said: A man came to Abdullah and said: “Should I perform the Witr prayer after the call to prayer? He said: Yes, and after the iqamah.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Al-Qasim was Ibn Ma'an was trustworthy, but he was a Murji'ah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1376","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Omar bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Omar bin Al Khattab, On the authority of Saeed bin Yassar, he said: Ibn Omar told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform the Witr prayer on a camel.”"
"1377","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abu Majliz, On the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Witr is a rak’ah at the end of the night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1378","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Na Yahya, and Muhammad, saying: Then he mentioned a word meaning: Na Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The Witr is a rak’ah at the end of the night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1379","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, on the authority of Affan, he said: Hammam, he said: Qatada, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the night prayer, and he said: “Two by two, and the Witr is a rak’ah at the end of the night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1380","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a reading of it, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, and Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about The night prayer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The night prayer is two by two, so if one of you fears the dawn, he prays one rak’ah, observing the Witr prayer.” He has what he has prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1381","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: We are Bishr, meaning Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: We are Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He did not say the salutation in the two rak’ahs of Witr.”"
"1382","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, he said: my father told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, he said: Ata’ told me Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The witr is a right, so whoever wishes, may perform the witr with five, and whoever wishes He may perform the Witr prayer with three, and whoever wishes may perform the Witr prayer with one.”"
"1383","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiyya told us, he said: Dabbarah bin Abi Al-Saleel told me, he said: Dawayd bin Nafi’ told me, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, he said: Ata’ bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Witr is true. Whoever wishes may pray the Witr with seven, and whoever wishes may pray the Witr with five, and whoever wishes may pray the Witr with three, and whoever wishes may pray the Witr with one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1384","Al-Harith bin Miskin said, I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: “ Whoever wishes, may pray the Witr with seven, and whoever wishes, may pray the Witr with five, and whoever wishes, may pray the Witr with three, and whoever is unable, nod with a nod.” Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: The One who is given the right is more deserving of what is right, and God knows best."
"1385","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, he said: Abu Mu’eed, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: Ata’ bin Yazid told me that he heard Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari say: “The witr is a right, so whoever loves to He prays the Witr with five rak’ahs, let him do so, and whoever likes to pray the Witr with three rak’ahs, let him do so, and whoever likes to pray the Witr with one rak’ah, let him do so.”"
"1386","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He should perform the Witr prayer with five and seven witr prayers, not separating them with a greeting or a word.”"
"1387","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar informed us, and said: Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Umm Salamah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform the Witr prayer with seven or five rak’ahs, not separating them with a salutation.”"
"1388","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Yazid, he said: I am Sufyan bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, he said: “The Witr Seven, and not less than five.” Al-Hakam said: So I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: From whom did he mention it? So I said: I do not know. Al-Hakam said: So I performed Hajj and found an divided person, so I said: From whom? He said: On the authority of Al-Thiqah, on the authority of Aisha and Maimuna. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1389","Ismail bin Masoud told me, he said: Yazid, who is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah, on the authority of al-Hakam, he said: I told Maqsam: I I hear the call to prayer, so I pray Witr with three, then I go out to pray for fear that I will miss it. He said: “That is not suitable except with seven or five.” So I told Mujahid and Yahya bin Al-Jazzar about that, and they said: Ask him, about whom? He said: So I asked him, and he said: On the authority of Al-Thiqah, on the authority of Aisha and Maimuna, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1390","And Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, saying: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to perform the Witr prayer with five prayers; he would not sit except in the last of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1391","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: I am Khalid, he said: we are Saeed, he said: we are Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, established the Sunnah and took the meat, he prayed seven rak’ahs, not sitting except in He lasted them, then he prayed two rak'ahs while sitting after the salutation, and that was nine, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer he loved to maintain it.”"
"1392","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: I am Ishaq, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin More fully, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became old and weak, he prayed the Witr prayer with seven rak’ahs; no He sits except at the sixth, then he gets up and does not say the salutation, so he prays the seventh, then he says the salutation, then he prays two rak’ahs while sitting.”"
"1393","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray the Witr prayer with nine rak’ahs, but when he meat, he prayed the Witr prayer with seven, and he bowed two rak’ahs while he was Sitting, “Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar example (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1394","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told me, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad. On the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray Witr with nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1395","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told me, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq On the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray Witr with nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1396","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said: I said: O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: We were preparing his ablution for him. And his siwak, then God will raise him up when He wishes to raise him during the night, so he will use his siwak and perform ablution, then he will pray nine rak’ahs, without sitting during them. Except at eight o'clock, then he praises his Lord, and supplicates and remembers Him, then he gets up and does not give the salutation, and prays the ninth hour, then he sits and remembers his Lord. And he praises Him, then he supplicates, then he says the salutation in a way that makes us hear, then he prays two rak’ahs while sitting, after he says the salutation, and that is one of the “Ten rak’ahs, my son.”"
"1397","Othman bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Harra, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to perform Witr with nine rak’ahs, sitting in the eighth, then he would get up and perform one rak’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1398","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said: I came to Medina, So I went to Aisha and said: Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was At night he prays the evening prayer, then he goes to bed and sleeps. When it is the middle of the night, he gets up to do what he needs and to purify himself. So he performed ablution, then entered the mosque, and prayed eight rak’ahs. It seemed to me that he was equal among them in recitation, bowing, and prostration, and praying the Witr prayer. One rak'ah, then he prayed two rak'ahs, while sitting, then he lay on his side. Perhaps Bilal came and called him to prayer before he fell asleep. And perhaps he fell asleep, and perhaps I doubted whether he had fallen asleep or not until he called him to prayer, and that was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until Sunnah. And meat, she said: He used to lead the people in the evening prayer, then he would go to bed, and when it was the middle of the night, he would get up to purify himself and take care of his needs. So he performed ablution, then entered the mosque and prayed six rak’ahs. It seemed to me that he was equal to them in recitation, bowing, and prostration, then he performed the Witr prayer. One rak'ah, then he prayed two rak'ahs while sitting, then he lay on his side. Perhaps Bilal came to him and called him to prayer before he fell asleep, and perhaps He fell asleep, and perhaps I doubted whether he had fallen asleep or not until he called him to prayer. She said: That was still the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1399","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubaid Allah, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Wathhab, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night, and she said: “Seven, nine, and eleven.” “Except the two rak’ahs of the morning.”"
"1400","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He used to pray eleven rak’ahs at night, of which he would pray Witr with one, and when he finished it, he would lie on his right side.”"
"1401","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night, then he would pray two light rak’ahs when he heard the call for dawn.”"
"1402","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night, performing Witr in them with five rak’ahs. He did not sit for any of the five rak’ahs, except in The last of them, then he sits, then he greets.”"
"1403","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, that He told him that he asked Aisha, the Mother of the Believers: How was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Ramadan? She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray more than eleven rak’ahs in Ramadan or at any other time, and he did not pray four.” Ask about their beauty and length, then he should pray four, but do not ask about their beauty and length, then he should pray three. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, do you sleep before praying the Witr prayer? He said: “O Aisha, my eyes sleep, but my heart does not sleep.”"
"1404","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hamza, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: You told me Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray eight rak’ahs after Isha’, then perform Witr, then pray two rak’ahs, reciting In them, he was sitting, so if he wanted to bow, he would stand up and bow, then after that he would bow the two rak’ahs of Fajr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1405","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Hanzalah, that he heard Al-Qasim, speaking, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would pray ten rak’ahs at night. He would pray Witr with one rak’ah, then perform the two rak’ahs of dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1406","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Abu al-Numan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Asim al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that Abu Musa was between Mecca and Medina, so he prayed the evening prayer with two rak’ahs, then he got up and prayed a rak’ah with which he performed Witr. So he recited one hundred verses from women, then said: “I would not wish to place my feet where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his feet, and to I recite what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited.”"
"1407","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: I was in the house of Maimuna, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed during the night, so I stood with him on his left, and he took my hand and made me \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1408","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: We have a partner, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “He used to recite the verse: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and say, ‘O disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, the One and Only’’” in one rak’ah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1409","Al-Hussein bin Issa told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told me, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite three strings, recited at the beginning with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and in The second: “Say, ‘O you disbelievers.” And the third: “Say, ‘He is God, One.’”"
"1410","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “ He used to pray Witr with three verses: “Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and say, ‘O disbelievers,’ and say, ‘He is God, One.’”"
"1411","Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Ibrahim bin Ishkaab told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Ubaidah told us, he said: Ubiyy told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Talha, On the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka`b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was It is recited in Witr prayer as: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and say, “O disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, the One.’” When he said the salaam, he said: “Glory be to the King.” “The Holy One” three times (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1412","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Numayr, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He used to recite in the Witr verse: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and say, ‘O you disbelievers,’ and say, ‘He is God.’” \"Sunday\""
"1413","Abdullah bin Al-Sabah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Habib told us, he said: Ruh bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Ata bin Al-Sa’ib, On the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to recite during the Witr prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord.” The highest, and say, “O disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, One.’” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1414","Ali bin Maimun Al-Raqi told us, he said: We are Mukhlid bin Yazid, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza. On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He used to pray Witr with three rak’ahs, reciting in the first with: ‘Glorify the name of God’. Your Lord is the Most High. And in the second verse, “Say, O you disbelievers.” And in the third, “Say, He is God, the One.” And he said in obedience before bowing. Then when he finished, When he finished, he said: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times, prolonging the last of them. Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by more than one person on the authority of Zubaid, and none of them mentioned about it: “He performs Qunoun before bowing.”"
"1415","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Lord, the Most High, and say, ‘O The disbelievers, and say, “He is God, One.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1416","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadah narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High,’ and say, ‘O you disbelievers,’ and say, ‘He is God, the One.’” Then, behold, He finished praying and said: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Shu`bah entered between Zubaid and Sa`id bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Abza Dhar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1417","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz, he said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Salamah, and Zubaid, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray Witr with: Praise the name of your Lord Most High and say, ‘O disbelievers,’ and say He is God, One, and he used to say: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times, and raise his voice the third time."
"1418","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not He raises his hands in any of his supplications, except when praying for rain.” Shu’bah said: So I said to Thabit: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to God. I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to God (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1419","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: Shu’bah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to raise his hands in supplication until the whites of his armpits could be seen.” Shu’bah said: So I came to Ali bin Zayd and mentioned that to him. He said: He only meant rain rain, so I said to him: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to God. I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Glory be to God. Abu Abdul Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by Qatada, on the authority of Anas."
"1420","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: narrated by Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: narrated by Shu’bah, he said: narrated by Qatada, that Anas bin Malik, He told them that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He did not raise his hands in any of his supplications, except when praying for rain; until the whites of his armpits can be seen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1421","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abd al-Razzaq, he said: Yunus bin Sulaym told us, he said: Yunus bin Yazid al-Ayli dictated to me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, who said: I heard Omar ibn al-Khattab, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Peace be upon him, when the revelation descended upon him, he would hear a noise like the sound of bees. We stayed for an hour, then he faced the Qiblah and raised his hands. And he said: “O God, increase us and do not diminish us, honor us and do not disgrace us, do not disgrace us, prefer us and do not favor us, be pleased with us and be pleased with us,” then He said: “Ten verses have been revealed to me. Whoever adheres to them will enter Paradise.” Then he read: “The believers have succeeded {1} those who are in their prayers.” They are humble {2}.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. We do not know of anyone who narrated it except Yunus bin Sulaym, and Yunus bin Sulaym we do not know. And God knows best"
"1422","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, he said: Abdul Rabbuh bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Imran Ibn Abi Anas, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Nafi’ Ibn Al-Amiya, on the authority of Rabi’ah Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Al-Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Prayer is two by two, you recite the Tashahhud in every two rak’ahs, you supplicate, you submit with humility, you remain still, and you fold your hands. He says: You raise them up to your Lord, facing Your face with their bellies, and say: O Lord, O Lord, whoever does not do such-and-such, means: \"prematurity\""
"1423","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sa`id bin Amir, he said: Shu`bah is us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Sa`id, on the authority of Anas bin Abi Anas On the authority of Abdullah bin Nafi’ bin Al-Amiya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Muttalib, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Prayer is two by two, and you recite the Tashahhud in every two rak’ahs, and stand still, and remain still, and fold your hands, and say: “O God, O God, so whoever does not If he does that, he is premature.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith other than al-Layth and Shu’bah on Their difference in it"
"1424","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Al-Hawza, Abu Abd said The Most Gracious: His name is Rabi’ah bin Shayban. He said: Al-Hasan bin Ali said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, taught me words that I should say in the Witr prayer.” Qunoot, O God, guide me among those whom You have guided, protect me from among those whom You have pardoned, take care of me among those whom You have appointed, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You are You will judge and it will not be judged against you, and none will be humiliated by those whom you have appointed. Blessed are you, and exalted are you, our Lord.”"
"1425","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Salem, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ali, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me these words in the Witr prayer. He said: “O God, guide me.” Among those whom You have guided, and bless for me what You have given, and take me as my ally among whomever You have taken care of, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed, for indeed You decree and He will not decree against you, and indeed He will not be humiliated. Whoever you have ruled over, you have blessed and exalted our Lord, and may God’s blessings and peace be upon Muhammad the Prophet.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1426","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, and Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, they said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Hisham bin Amr Al-Fazari, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him: He used to say at the end of his Witr prayer, “O God, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You, I cannot count Praise be to you, just as you praised yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1427","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Laith told us, he said: Uqail told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray eleven rak’ahs, between finishing the evening prayer until dawn.” At night, except for the two dawn rak’ahs, and prostrate as much as one of you recites, fifty verses.”"
"1428","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Ezra, speaking, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: Praise the name of your Lord Most High and say, O The disbelievers, and say: He is God, the One. Then when he finished, he said: “Glory be to the King, the Holy” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1429","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Zurarah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He used to pray Witr to glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and say, ‘O you disbelievers, and say, He is God. Someone, when he greets him, says: “Glory be to the Holy King” three times, and extends it the third time."
"1430","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad al-Muddab Harami told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: I heard Zubaid speaking, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the string with: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord. The highest, and say, “O disbelievers,” and say, “He is God, the One.” When he greeted, he said, “Glory be to the King, the Holy,” three times, extending his voice in The third, and it is raised (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1431","Ubayd Allah ibn Faddalah al-Nasa’i told me. He said: I am Muhammad, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak. He said: We are Muawiyah, and he is Ibn Salam ibn Abi Salam al-Habashi. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Abu Salam’s name is Mutur, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, He asked Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the night. She said: “He used to pray thirteen days during the night.” One rak'ah, nine rak'ahs standing, and he performs Witr in them, and two rak'ahs sitting, so if he wants to bow, he stands, bows, prostrates, and does That is after Witr. When he hears the call to Fajr, he gets up and performs two short rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1432","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Othman bin Omar, who is Ibn Faris, Basri, told us, he said: Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He would not omit four rak’ahs before noon, and two rak’ahs before noon.” Before dawn.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith has not been followed up by anyone, according to what he said, on the authority of Masruq. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1433","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad, that he heard his father, He heard Aisha say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not omit four rak’ahs before noon and two rak’ahs before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1434","Harun bin Ishaq told us, he said: I am Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Two dawn prayers are better than the whole world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1435","Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: I read to Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiya, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray the two rak’ahs of dawn, two short rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1436","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: I am Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that Hafsa, the mother of The believers told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “When the muezzin was silent for the morning call to prayer, and dawn began, he would pray two rak’ahs.” two light prayers, before the prayer begins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1437","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent for the first part of the Fajr prayer, he would get up and prostrate two light rak’ahs before Fajr prayer, after the dawn is clearly evident, then he lies on his right side.”"
"1438","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salat, Kufi told us, he said: Abu Kudaynah told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to lie down after the two rak’ahs of dawn on his right side, then sit Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Kudaynah’s name is Yahya ibn al-Muhallab. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1439","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of a man, who had satisfaction, who told him, Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no one who prays at night, but he is overcome by it.” Sleeping, except that the reward for his prayer is recorded for him, and his sleep is a charity given to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1440","Abu Dawud told us: Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Abi Dawud, and he was called an owl, there is nothing wrong with him, and his father is neither trustworthy nor trustworthy. Mamoun, he said: Abu Ja`far al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Yazid, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever misses a prayer, prays it during the night and falls asleep, that is a charity that God has given him charity.” And the reward for his prayers is recorded for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1441","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Husayn bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abdah bin Abi Lubaba, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of it. He said: “Whoever comes He was in his bed, intending to get up and pray during the night, but his eyes clouded his mind until morning. What he intended was recorded for him, and his sleep was a charity given to him. From his Lord.” Sufyan al-Thawri and Sufyan bin Uyaynah disagreed with him. Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, On the authority of Abdah, he said: I heard Suwayd bin Ghafla, and Suwayd told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Lubaba, On the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, on the authority of Abu Dharr, or on the authority of Abu Darda’, it is authenticated. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1442","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If he did not pray during the night, he would be prevented from doing so by sleep that overcame his eyes, or pain, so he would pray during the day.” Twelve rak'ahs\""
"1443","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Safwan Abdullah bin Saeed bin Abdul Malik bin Marwan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid and Ubayd Allah told him that Abdul-Rahman bin Abdul-Qari said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever falls asleep and misses his party, or any part of it, and recites it between the dawn prayer and the noon prayer, it is written. It is as if he had read it at night.”"
"1444","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, and Ubaid Allah, told him that Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abdul, said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab, saying: “Whoever falls asleep from his party, or from any part of it, and recites it in between the prayer The dawn and noon prayers were written for him as if he had recited them during the night.”"
"1445","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, that Omar ibn al-Khattab said: “Whoever sleeps and misses his part, or he said: his part of the night, recites it in between the morning prayer to the noon prayer, as if he had recited it during the night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1446","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abdul-Qari, that Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said: “Whoever misses his party at night, and recites it when the sun goes down to the noon prayer, he has not missed it or as if he had missed it.” \"He overtook him\""
"1447","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, that Omar, He said: “Whoever missed it at night, let him recite it in the prayer before noon, for it is equivalent to the night prayer.”"
"1448","Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Mughirah bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is persistent in praying twelve rak’ahs a day and a night will enter Paradise: Four rak’ahs before noon, two rak’ahs after it, two rak’ahs after sunset, two rak’ahs after the evening prayer, and two rak’ahs before dawn.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is a mistake, and perhaps he meant Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, so he corrected it."
"1449","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Maqsimi told me, he said: Hajjaj told me, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, I said to Ata’: I have been informed that you bow before Twelve rak'ahs on Friday. Have you heard any news about that? He said: Umm Habiba Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan informed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kneels twelve rak’ahs in... “Today and tonight are other than the written ones. God will build for him a house in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1450","Ayoub bin Muhammad al-Wazzan told me, he said: we are Muammar bin Sulaiman, he said: we are Zaid, and he is Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever prays on the day of “Ten rak’ahs, God built a house for him in Paradise.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Ata’ bin Abi Rabah did not hear it from Anbasa. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1451","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, he said: Zayd ibn Hubab told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sa’id al-Taifi told me, he said: I am Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ya`la ibn Umayyah said: I entered Taif and saw Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan while he was dying, and I saw his distress, so I said: You are To the best, and he said: My sister Umm Habiba told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs during the day Or at night, a house was built for him in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1452","Muhammad ibn Hatim ibn Nu`aym informed us, saying: We are Hibban, and Muhammad ibn Makki, saying: I am Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Abu Yunus al-Qushayri. On the authority of Ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Shahr ibn Hawshab, on the authority of Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, she said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs in... One day, he prayed before noon, and God built a house for him in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1453","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Jizzi told me, he said: Abu Al-Aswad told me, he said: Bakr bin Mudar told me, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Amr ibn Aws, on the authority of Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs, a house will be built for him in Paradise: four rak’ahs before noon, and two rak’ahs after noon.” “Two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer, two rak’ahs after the sunset prayer, and two rak’ahs before the morning prayer.”"
"1454","Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Anbasa, my brother Umm Habibah, on the authority of Umm Habibah, said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs today and night other than the prescribed ones, a house will be built for him in Paradise: four rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after it, two before the afternoon, two after sunset, and two \"before dawn\""
"1455","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yazid, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs during the day and night, a house will be built for him in \"Paradise\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1456","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ya’la told us, Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habibah said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs day or night, apart from the obligatory prayers, a house will be built for him in Paradise,” said Abu Abd al-Rahman: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman entered between al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’ and Anbasa Dhakwan, and he did not transmit the hadith."
"1457","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Wahb bin Baqiya told me, he said: I am Khalid, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ubayy Saleh Dhakwan said: Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan told me that Umm Habibah told him that: “Whoever prays on the day of twelve one rak’ah, a house will be built for him in Paradise.”"
"1458","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Habibah, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs on a day other than the obligatory prayer, God will build for him or a house will be built for him in Paradise,” said Abu Abdul Rahman: This hadith was narrated by Suhail bin Abi Saleh, and there was disagreement over it."
"1459","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya bin Ishaq told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs on a day other than the obligatory ones, God will build for him a house in “Paradise.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I think this hadith is a mistake, and Muhammad bin Sulaiman is weak, and Falayh bin Sulaiman disagreed with it, so he narrated it. On the authority of Suhail bin Abi Ishaq (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1460","Ahmad bin Al-Azhar told us, he said: Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Fulayh told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Umm Habiba, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs, God will build a house for him.” In Paradise: four before noon, two after it, two before afternoon, two after sunset, and two before In the morning, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct in our view, and Fulayh bin Suleiman is not strong in hadith, and God knows best, and he This hadith was narrated by Hassan bin Atiyya, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, without this wording. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1461","Yazid bin Muhammad bin Abdul Samad told me, he said: Hisham Al-Attar told me, he said: Ismail, who is the son of Abdullah bin Sama’ah, told me, on the authority of Musa bin Ayan, on the authority of Abu Amr, who is Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiya, he said: When he descended on Anbasa, he began to starve, so it was said to him, and he said: As for me, I heard Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Who He prayed four rak’ahs before noon, and four after it. God burned his flesh over the fire. “So I have not left them since I heard them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1462","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Marwan bin Muhammad, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, Marwan said: He was happy when it was read to him, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, acknowledged that and did not deny it, and if he told us about it, he did not raise it. She said: “Whoever kneels four rak’ahs before noon, And four after that, God will make him forbidden to the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1463","Abdullah bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, he said: I heard Suleiman bin Musa speaking, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Sufyan said: When death befell him, a severe matter seized him, and he said: My sister, Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan, told me: She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever performs four rak’ahs before noon and four after it, God will condemn him to the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1464","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, Maqil told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I was informed, that Umm Habiba The daughter of Abu Sufyan, she said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever kneels twelve rak’ahs in his day or night except written, God will build a house for him in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1465","Ahmad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, Abu Yahya Ishaq bin Sulayman al-Razi told me, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Ziyad. On the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever, meaning, prayed twelve rak’ahs, built God has a home for him in Paradise: four rak’ahs before noon, two rak’ahs after noon, two rak’ahs after sunset, and two rak’ahs after the evening prayer, And two rak’ahs before dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1466","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, my father told us, Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Zaid, Ayyub, a man from the Levant, told me on the authority of Al-Qasim Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, said: My sister, Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that Her beloved, Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no believing servant who prays four rak’ahs in the afternoon, and his face is touched by fire.” \"Never\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1467","Amr bin Ali told us, Abu Qutaybah told me, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sha’ithi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays four times before noon and four after it, the fire will not touch him.” \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1468","Ahmad bin Nasih told us, Marwan bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Sulayman bin Musa, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Umm Habiba, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Whoever prays four rak’ahs before noon and four After that, God will burn him with fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1469","Ibn Al-Muthanna narrated to us, Suwayd, who is Ibn Amr, narrated to us, Hammad narrated to me, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs a day, God will build for him a house in Paradise.”"
"1470","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, Ibn Makki and Hibban informed us, they said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, He mentioned on the authority of Umm Habiba, who said: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs in a day or night other than the prescribed ones, God will build for him a house in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1471","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz delayed the prayer a little, and Urwa said to him: As for Gabriel, he descended and prayed before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Omar said: I know what you are saying, Urwa. He said: I heard Bashir bin Abu Masoud saying: I heard Abu Masoud saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Gabriel came down and gave me security, so I prayed with him.” Then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, then I prayed with him, and he counted five prayers with his fingers.”"
"1472","Anba Kathir bin Ubaid Al-Humsi told us: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Anas bin Malik told me that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He went out when the sun had risen and led the noon prayer with them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1473","Anba Ubaid Allah bin Saeed said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Hamza Al-A’idhi told me, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “Whenever he settled at a certain place, he would not move on until he had prayed the noon prayer.” A man said to him: “And if In the middle of the day? He said: “Even if it is in the middle of the day?”"
"1474","I am Ubayd Allah bin Saeed. He said: Abu Saeed, the client of Banu Hashim, told us. He said: Khalid bin Dinar Abu Khalda told us. He said: I heard Anas. Ibn Malik said: “When it was hot, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to cool himself off with prayer, and when it was cold he would hasten it.”"
"1475","On the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Khaldah, Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Anas: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When the cold becomes severe, he prays early and prays early, and when the heat becomes intense, he cools himself off with prayer. The beginning of it is: Al-Hakam ibn Ayyub delayed the Friday prayer. Then Yazid al-Dhabi spoke (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1476","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Humsi told us, he said: Othman told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salama told me, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When the heat is severe, then cool off from prayer, for the severity of “Free from the stench of hell” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1477","Qutayba bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, and the wording for it, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the heat becomes intense, cool off with prayer, for the intensity of the heat is from the stench of Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1478","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When the heat becomes intense, refrain from praying, for the intensity of the heat is a result of the stench of Hell.”"
"1479","Anba Amr bin Mansour told us: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Yazid bin Aws, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Musa, narrating it, said: “Cool down at noon, for what you find of the heat comes from the stench of Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1480","Abba Yaqoub bin Ibrahim said: Abba Humayd bin Abd Larahman said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahb, on the authority of Khabbab said: “We complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about Hurr al-Ramdha, but he did not complain.”"
"1481","Anba Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Ubaidah ibn Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik al-Ashja’i Sa’d. Ibn Tariq, on the authority of Kathir Ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Al-Aswad Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, who said: “The prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May God bless him and grant him peace: In the summer it is three to five feet at noon, and in the winter it is five to seven feet. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1482","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported to Abu Ammar, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “This is Gabriel, who came to you to teach you your religion. He prayed the morning prayer when dawn came, and he prayed the noon prayer when the sun had risen.” Then he prayed the afternoon prayer when he saw a similar shadow, then he prayed the sunset prayer when the sun had set and the fasting person had broken his fast, then he prayed the evening prayer when twilight had gone. night, then tomorrow came, and he prayed the morning prayer for him when it had spread a little, then he prayed the noon prayer when the shadow was like it, then he prayed the afternoon prayer when the shadow was twice, then he prayed the Maghrib prayer at the same time, when the sun had set and the fasting person had broken his fast, then he prayed the evening prayer when an hour of the night had passed, Then he said: The prayer is between your prayer yesterday and your prayer today. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1483","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He prayed the afternoon prayer while the sun was in its room, and the fay did not appear.”"
"1484","Anba Qutaibah bin Saeed said: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he informed him: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, “He used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was high and alive, and the one who went to high places would go while the sun was high.”"
"1485","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Uthman bin Sahl bin Hanif, saying: I heard Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, saying: We prayed the noon prayer with Omar bin Abdul Aziz, then we went out until we entered Anas bin Malik, and we found him praying the afternoon prayer. I said: Uncle, what is this prayer that you prayed? He said: “Asr, and this is the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which we used to pray with him.”"
